 "▼ Dive in: <0>Comparison table</0>": "",
 "Each mechanism answers a different question: <0>what to know</0> (skill, prompt), <1>what to do</1> (tool, MCP), <2>who does it</2> (sub-agent), <3>how the model behaves</3> (fine-tuning).": "",
 "They combine well: a skill can tell the agent which tools to call and in which order.": "",
 "Rule of thumb: start with the cheapest, most editable option (prompt → skill → tool) and only fine-tune if that is not enough.": "",
 "The table is a simplification; real products blur these boundaries.": "",
